[{"id":"VRCE-2-81-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing the words of Guha, exceedingly unpleasant, Bharata as soon as he heard them, became plunged in thought.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1bb0c2d0778aa22fbf210edda14f2318dde3e6b959eda37fd3fe623d47a0bcfc","compact":"0c77c7ede2e12964eeaba511ec98687e3b87f6c10630034f77e6d176bfb8a9d5","nasal":"0c77c7ede2e12964eeaba511ec98687e3b87f6c10630034f77e6d176bfb8a9d5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":2,"english":"And then taking heart for a while, that tenderfamed one possessed of immense strength, gifted with leonine shoulders and length of arms, having expansive eyes resembling white lotuses, young in years, and endowed with a handsome presence, afflicted with great grief, was overpowered, like an elephant wounded in the heart with a goad.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c54d1b39392fc7b85c4859bb81d8c00f525b3331874d45a009513cd411b8c11f","compact":"db2af6ea3cc09b01c85addbc35936dcdb95679f5c0700bf9ea87b6bc2bf11aa5","nasal":"40dfa7672d2ee8b893251fe923af18c36106ceb033e95e805c0b152a715240aa"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":3,"english":"And then taking heart for a while, that tenderfamed one possessed of immense strength, gifted with leonine shoulders and length of arms, having expansive eyes resembling white lotuses, young in years, and endowed with a handsome presence, afflicted with great grief, was overpowered, like an elephant wounded in the heart with a goad.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.703,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"105365182e689cc55538f8dac2ceb09091c9c2829de661596f82178286b44012","compact":"6750584ff0b838cd02725ebb0dc2b09eb18fe51a4fff1a7e60754c8aacf88d14","nasal":"6750584ff0b838cd02725ebb0dc2b09eb18fe51a4fff1a7e60754c8aacf88d14"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":4,"english":"Seeing Bharata in that condition, ſatrughna who was near, taking the former on his lap, began to cry, almost deprived of his senses and oppressed with grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"705af13a712e58ff36c7f89a7ace6525ccb9a6fb6aa348879a28795d29880cd4","compact":"69f8292f972f10c166ab3e927288c49abfcf842fc1271440d56cdb07d000b6ef","nasal":"4fb8f164f9329d7983aa29f73f21fa2e8bd86520c27d7593a023247b52626cc1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":5,"english":"Thereat, all the mothers of Bharata, fasting, undergoing distress, and afflicted with the calamity that had befallen their lord, came forward, and surrounding Bharata, began to lament him fallen on the ground. And the distressed Kausalyā drawing nigh embraced him like a cow approaching her calf; and weeping from excess of grief, spoke to Bharata, saying.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e2d594c3fbc3524c357ce8738e09d507ad9c821eda0f4cb8374cb42058260f19","compac