d1f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":8,"english":"My son, does any malady afflict your body? Now the life of this royal race is, without doubt, in your hands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.619,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bbc5bc7ad9c994867d624c573a899838a2eef25eec0b5061de8e6cf168ba2977","compact":"39c3e7afe19bac70b4dad34e49de277394955819e4a4ef7961136f141c000b44","nasal":"39c3e7afe19bac70b4dad34e49de277394955819e4a4ef7961136f141c000b44"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":9,"english":"Ráma having gone away along with his brother, I shall, O son, live, seeing you. King Dasaratha having departed this life, you alone are our lord.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"180683ea61839f054dc0c2b431eb14a3a8bfcaae980984a1fdf225c5e4859234","compact":"51418c37be53305742a3cf81ff3908d8789d243010396b18555170a65436d5f6","nasal":"51418c37be53305742a3cf81ff3908d8789d243010396b18555170a65436d5f6"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":10,"english":"Have you, my son, heard anything unpleasant concerning Lakṣmaṇa; or the son of that one having an only son,* who has gone to the forest along with his wife? *Meaning herself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.9,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b8de0d426c8b9253fba4f9b18410d842b6d36c2e3b8353c289f4b2ea46546a9f","compact":"363f9faf5642720dd10016c7fea384825d86c8b1989e56be2a1f0912e9c155fd","nasal":"001ed945529e0f97d4fb231d329d65f9090bdfb7bc46e36d7b75099ae16f76a9"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":11,"english":"Having taken comfort for a while, that one of high fame weeping, and solacing Kausalya, spoke to Guha, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6295bf9b8210c82b60aa07f90f2fd9c49ffb4cb5e32dce7c9e5e7841e83295fb","compact":"27a8d0e6d1abcaee78510c6b9e0bdd93b76b6bef3f64c19cc0f51091658bde51","nasal":"a1270143f31b7b7dd403d6133accd2c87a110d4b6ebe773ff5f2dcf7b8894348"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":12,"english":"Where did my brother pass the night? And where did Sītā? And where did, again, Laks maņa? And in what bed did he sleep, and what did he previously partake of? Do you, O Guha, tell me this.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5a6a72ce225a9dff4f2ebd79bcb2c1dc4c0a3e65c65105f9824b432d68c34e78","compact":"db7a91f7e511d65eaa59a4357bf14060055c444a5810c23bd5d8e54612ebc36c","nasal":"db7a91f7e511d65eaa59a4357bf14060055c444a5810c23bd5d8e54612ebc36c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":13,"english":"Thereat, well pleased, Gulha, the lord of Nişādas, related to Bharata how he had acted in respect of Rāma, his dear guest, studious of his welfare.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ff379d3d3b73a188e1dfe0027d43bf23bfebb6840955034d14f97fe79a9e4f52","compact":"89abef94a70aa44153ae368cb3678a789f58a55e99a19ac7591b71de9c329ad9","nasal":"89abef94a70aa44153ae368cb3678a789f58a55e99a19ac7591b71de9c329ad9"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":14,"english":"I procured for Rāma's use rice and fruits and roots and various kinds of food.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aa777d9302499949d224ac70af11faac111d0bcf40b2d1a0e7b957699e1ada8f","compact":"03362424cb3d60a314bc0732107242500818a972c8855a12a854c049a796aa5b","nasal":"7cb9ef9bb0e0739f5e8cd3dbfcb0484f65ad205d3824620c971610abbcc42ce4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":15,"english":"All these Rāma having truth for his prowess accepted, but observing Ksatriya morality, he did not take them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.849,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"042ab040330d6c70db642d41f232511cbd33def997502903a93c541abc7c5250","compact":"24c689e09f61f67f51c309735d7e62c57881933470cfdbeab4e3d45036bbfbf4","nasal":"24c689e09f61f67f51c309735d7e62c57881933470cfdbeab4e3d45036bbfbf4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":16,"english":"'O friend, we ought not to take anything: ours is always to give.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.787,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"242401e8fa535f545b4ea755585901d1348d7a4814ac01996da9f3eb109a35f2","compact":"607fd610f701f2a57ff172e8ecb3f1b64a16a285cbf57082d551c287ae762936","nasal":"b654fba04a514bc972ad1aedaedf9ff6f5ed6e3188b9d5a170377c6e281f0d29"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":17,"english":"Thus did that magnanimous one beseech us. On the high-souled Lakşmaņa bringing water, Rāghava having drunk it, fasted along with Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.333,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3784c56ec2ed1e85afc027d871c1ac195bf6d8b008a94aadaf751ef69e76d4c3","compact":"c08b787fac8da5d311b5e549c295b6e08e9436a214043bb65cfbcd6fa2fe144b","nasal":"c08b787fac8da5d311b5e549c295b6e08e9436a214043bb65cfbcd6fa2fe144b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":18,"english":"Then Lakşmaņa drank up the water that remained. Then the three with fixed minds silently performed their adorations to the Twilight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.77,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bafc9104bae6a0ff44e3129168b83fb6072fb17395cbf6fa1f7b01fb65f1057b","compact":"9624dcdb43fa27155f03d6d2927e850c9a573de9b34c186f5289f9b07aacae95","nasal":"9624dcdb43fa27155f03d6d2927e850c9a573de9b34c186f5289f9b07aacae95"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":19,"english":"After that, Sumitrā's son prepared a goodly bed for Rāghava, himself bringing Kuća grass.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d2b9a7a17abddc6ddc372a86e09398e4c9b62c859c106a7dd5b3907288ba5882","compact":"6c36bef0c2c721032061fc6b606d23f5611ebfde3d0ba267b6428a819ab0a43e","nasal":"6c36bef0c2c721032061fc6b606d23f5611ebfde3d0ba267b6428a819ab0a43e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":20,"english":"And in that bed lay down Rāma in company with Sītā. Next washing their feet, Lakşmaņa turned away.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0d21e7aa440d81bdbb32eaa85b790a68654c6c00860972d2e229fa21643ec2ac","compact":"a8cba5fffa6dc4afd0d4f4b6cf60129409476965cad80b7604b86ce34cda0fca","nasal":"a8cba5fffa6dc4afd0d4f4b6cf60129409476965cad80b7604b86ce34cda0fca"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":21,"english":"This is the foot of the Ingudī, and this that grass. On it both Rāma and Sītā lay down that night.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"71a5e81f4846d1098db9c001e31d7297bb949a146d1d9bf9d166dc52554eda0b","compact":"f654ee00ab1d175d9b4a44bddbb8f88a472e78e6dbfc2e9a7b0f6ec79dd28b47","nasal":"8d000484502bbb57d79c31e2d0144dd08df73a30dd39529a970b16ec0020a4f2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":22,"english":"Fastening on his back a pair of quivers filled with arrows furnished with finger-fences, and taking his mighty bow, Lakşmaņa all night kept watch around.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.62,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b847d35d5de5421e2a1ba355d57524dbb132aebd06986487a34008c741c4bfe2","compact":"e2349ba0091bfec2adea92f3ef9944b10919c3c48150b69cd423ffc43ce9d283","nasal":"7898aa24b1bb175ad4e5803fa1fe137cda1e8bef4adfc10bd76aedf7d401b49c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-81-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":81,"verse":23,"english":"I also taking an excellent bow, remained where remained Lakṣmaṇa, and surrounded by my kindred who stayed there vigilantly, equipped with bows, guarded him that resembled the mighty Indra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.505,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-87-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2081023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"055f531996b24834e2a6681ec55de0761b1ac122368cb4a96e9919eab47bfd25","compact":"b4549fe8046be9e5513f91d4d3caeb4e5384d8d4d3c2b16036aabad635664ff4","nasal":"9b3cd785613c502cdb4ec2826f798f03d20b11b13de20e7c0e962ec80445ac9e"}}]
